            {
              "id": "0ff09ed7-cee4-34ce-b886-0ee9f79ba46d",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"Implementation of Vulnerable Cryptography Hash Function\" vulnerability refers to the use of weak or broken cryptographic hash functions in a C++ program. Cryptographic hash functions are used to convert input data into a fixed size hash value, which is typically used for data integrity checks and password storage. If a weak or broken hash function is used, it can lead to various security issues such as data tampering, password cracking, and other forms of attacks.\n\nIn the provided code snippet, the `STEP` function is a part of an implementation of the MD5 hash function. MD5 is considered to be a weak hash function as it is vulnerable to hash collisions, where different input data can produce the same hash value.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to use a strong and secure hash function such as SHA-256 or SHA-3. These hash functions are currently considered to be secure and are not known to have any significant vulnerabilities.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nReplace the MD5 hash function with a secure hash function. Here is an example of how to use the SHA-256 hash function in C++:\n\n```cpp\n#include <openssl/sha.h>\n#include <string>\n\nstd::string sha256(const std::string str)\n{\n    unsigned char hash[SHA256_DIGEST_LENGTH];\n    SHA256_CTX sha256;\n    SHA256_Init(&sha256);\n    SHA256_Update(&sha256, str.c_str(), str.size());\n    SHA256_Final(hash, &sha256);\n    std::stringstream ss;\n    for(int i = 0; i < SHA256_DIGEST_LENGTH; i++)\n    {\n        ss << std::hex << std::setw(2) << std::setfill('0') << (int)hash[i];\n    }\n    return ss.str();\n}\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe above code requires the OpenSSL library to execute properly.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Cryptographic Storage Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cryptographic_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/327.html)"
              },
